>  No signal at all from the SPDIF Toslink port! The reason trying this
> pin is that when overridden, it shows "SPDIF Out".

If so, the pin can be simply wrong.  Usually when a PCM stream starts
and "IEC958 Playback Switch" is on, the signal comes up.

You need to figure out which pin is connected to SPDIF.
(And note that it's not necessarily the Realtek codec that is
 connected to SPDIF, although it's very likely.)

Or, there can be some vendor-specific verb, GPIO, vref or whatever
non-standard control for enabling the SPDIF in addition.

Both above can be figured out only by the h/w owner -- or maybe better
to ask the hardware vendor about it.


Takashi

